{
  "_why": "O-Prism's getPresetListWithCategories returns a JSON STRING (Source/PluginEditor.cpp), not the juce::var object O-Bells returns. The generic stub defaults to the object because a page that JSON.parses one catches and degrades, while a page that Object.keys a string renders one bogus category per character. This file supplies Prism's real shape so its page boots without a console error. v1.21.0 adds two more: the generic stub returns an EMPTY getEmbeddedTuningList and an EMPTY getUserWavetableList, and a harness that cannot reach a state certifies nothing about it (the O-MicrotonalSampler lesson) - with both empty, the whole Tuning Library panel, the user-wavetable rows and the Manage.../Delete captions were never rendered and therefore never measured by check-ui-labels. The values below are the shape a loaded plugin carries. TEST FIXTURE ONLY - never shipped, never embedded. v1.21.0 also adds startWavetableEditor: without it the generic stub returns null, numFrames stays 0, and the Wavetable tab's frame strip and harmonic editor paint NOTHING - which made the fillText probe's own negative control fail to fire (a planted English canvas string went unreported because the painter never ran). getAllEditorFrameWaveforms and getFrameHarmonics are needed for the same reason: drawFrameStrip() only runs from getAllEditorFrameWaveforms' own .then().",
